> What is the "protection racket"?
> 

Original definition/proposal for the Nethack 'opening' called "The 
Protection Racket" from "The Nethack Book of Openings" can be found in 
this post:
news:<3BBECAE7.6F7F131C@bigpond.com>

AFAIK it was the only opening that ever got properly added to the 
'book'. The Racket has been the source of continuous discussion since.

The poster to this thread using the pseudonym 'none' outlines an 
interesting strategy of his own that seems to be based on the original 
Protection Racket opening (ie according to the post referenced above) 
but with lots of fleshing out that doesn't necessarily seem to be in 
line with the original idea. You will find a lot of people has different 
ideas about what the Protection Racket is, as can be seen from the 
responses in this thread.

